msgid "How Bloknote works & Contributing"
msgstr "How Bloknote works & Contributing"

#: src/routes/docs/+page.svelte
msgid "Bloknote is a static, offline-capable climbing directory built entirely on open data. There is no proprietary central database: routes, crags, sectors, and gyms live on <0>OpenStreetMap</0>, topo photos live on <1>Wikimedia Commons</1>, and personal ticks or reviews belong to your own <2>Atmosphere (AT Protocol)</2> repository."
msgstr "Bloknote is a static, offline-capable climbing directory built entirely on open data. There is no proprietary central database: routes, crags, sectors, and gyms live on <0>OpenStreetMap</0>, topo photos live on <1>Wikimedia Commons</1>, and personal ticks or reviews belong to your own <2>Atmosphere (AT Protocol)</2> repository."

#: src/routes/docs/+page.svelte
msgid "Static builds & offline SQLite cache"
msgstr "Static builds & offline SQLite cache"

#: src/routes/docs/+page.svelte
msgid "A scheduled pipeline compiles worldwide Overpass climbing data and regional GeoJSON boundaries into static JSON endpoints. In your browser, Bloknote downloads this snapshot into a local WebAssembly SQLite database so tree browsing, filtering, and diagnostics work instantaneously—even offline."
msgstr "A scheduled pipeline compiles worldwide Overpass climbing data and regional GeoJSON boundaries into static JSON endpoints. In your browser, Bloknote downloads this snapshot into a local WebAssembly SQLite database so tree browsing, filtering, and diagnostics work instantaneously—even offline."

